# =============================================================================
# Nuitka Build Configuration for El-Joumla ERP
# إعدادات بناء Nuitka لنظام الجملة
# =============================================================================
#
# This file documents the Nuitka build configuration used by scripts/build.py.
# Nuitka does not natively read .nuitka config files — all options are passed
# via the command line in build.py. This file serves as a human-readable
# reference and can be adapted into a Nuitka --user-package-configuration
# YAML if needed in the future.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project Info
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Application : El-Joumla ERP (نظام إدارة المبيعات والمجوز بالجملة)
#   Version     : 6.0.0
#   Company     : Standard El-Joumla
#   UI Framework: PySide6 (Qt 6)
#   Entry Point : main.py
#   Target OS   : Windows 10/11
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build Modes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. ONEFILE  (--onefile)
#    Produces a single self-extracting .exe.
#    Pros : Easy distribution, one file to ship.
#    Cons : Slower startup (unpacks to temp), larger binary, harder to debug.
#    Use  : Quick demos, portable USB distribution.
#
# 2. STANDALONE (--standalone)
#    Produces a folder with .exe + all dependencies.
#    Pros : Fast startup, easier debugging, InnoSetup installer support.
#    Cons : Multiple files to distribute.
#    Use  : Production deployments, installer creation.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Key Nuitka Options (as passed in build.py)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   --onefile / --standalone          Build mode selector
#   --enable-qt=pyside6               Enable PySide6 plugin (auto-includes Qt)
#   --windows-disable-console         Hide console window on launch
#   --windows-icon-from-ico=...       Application icon (.ico)
#   --windows-company-name=...        Company name in EXE metadata
#   --windows-product-name=...        Product name in EXE metadata
#   --windows-file-version=...        File version (e.g. 6.0.0)
#   --windows-product-version=...     Product version
#   --output-filename=...             Output EXE name (onefile mode)
#   --output-dir=...                  Output directory (standalone mode)
#   --include-data-dir=src=dst        Embed data directories at build time
#   --assume-yes-for-downloads        Auto-accept dependency downloads (MSVC, etc.)
#   --show-progress                   Display compilation progress
#   --show-memory                     Show memory usage during compilation
#   --python-flag=no_site            Skip site.py at runtime (faster startup)
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data Directories Included
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   assets/    → Icons, images, QSS stylesheets, font files
#   locales/   → Arabic/English translation .qm files
#   config/    → app_config.json, dev_config.json
#   data/      → Default data files, user_behavior.json
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# InnoSetup Installer (standalone mode only)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# After a standalone build, build.py can generate an installer.iss script.
# Run with:  iscc installer.iss
#
#   Output     : ElJoumla_Setup_6.0.0.exe
#   Compression: LZMA2 Ultra64 with solid compression
#   Languages  : Arabic + English
#   Features   : Desktop icon, start menu entry, auto-launch after install
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prerequisites
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   1. Python 3.10+ with all project dependencies installed
#   2. Nuitka:           pip install nuitka
#   3. PySide6:          pip install PySide6
#   4. C compiler:       MSVC (auto-downloaded by Nuitka) or MinGW64
#   5. InnoSetup 6:      https://jrsoftware.org/isdl.php  (optional, for installer)
#   6. Application icon: assets/icons/app_icon.ico
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quick Start
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   Onefile build:
#       python scripts/build.py --mode onefile
#
#   Standalone build + installer:
#       python scripts/build.py --mode standalone --installer
#
#   Clean + build both modes:
#       python scripts/build.py --mode both --clean --installer
#
# =============================================================================
